@startuml sequence_fleet_connect
!theme plain
title Fleet Connect Sequence (GUI → Bridge → FleetWebAPI)

participant "User" as user
participant "FleetDashboard\n(FleetDashboard.js)" as dashboard
participant "FleetClient\n(FleetClient.js)" as client
participant "FastAPI Bridge\n(localhost:1112)" as bridge
participant "FleetWebAPI\n(localhost:2510)" as fleet_api
participant "FleetOrchestrator" as orch

== 1. User Enters Fleet URL and Clicks Connect ==

user -> dashboard : Enter "http://localhost:2510"\nand click Connect
activate dashboard

dashboard -> client : configure("http://localhost:2510")
activate client

client -> client : _fleetApiUrl = "http://localhost:2510"

client -> bridge : POST /api/fleet/config\n{ fleet_api_url: "http://localhost:2510" }
activate bridge
note right of client
  **_bridgeOrigin()** resolves bridge URL:
  - Browser: MM.serviceClient.apiUrl
  - Electron: fallback to http://localhost:1112
end note

bridge -> bridge : bridge._fleet_api_url\n= "http://localhost:2510"
bridge --> client : { fleet_api_url: "http://localhost:2510" }
deactivate bridge

client --> dashboard : Promise resolved
deactivate client

dashboard -> dashboard : localStorage.setItem(\n'mm_fleet_api_url', url)
dashboard -> dashboard : showToast("Fleet Connected")

== 2. Register Callback and Start Polling ==

dashboard -> client : onUpdate(onFleetUpdate)
note right of dashboard
  Registers the dashboard's
  **onFleetUpdate** callback
  to receive poll results.
end note

dashboard -> client : startPolling()
activate client

client -> client : stopPolling() (clear old timer)
client -> client : poll()  (immediate first fetch)

== 3. First Poll — Proxied Through Bridge ==

client -> bridge : GET /api/fleet/status
activate bridge
note right of client
  All fleet calls go through the bridge.
  **_resolveUrl(path)** returns:
  _bridgeOrigin() + "/api/fleet/status"
end note

bridge -> bridge : Check bridge._fleet_api_url\nis set → proxy request

bridge -> fleet_api : GET http://localhost:2510/api/fleet/status
activate fleet_api

fleet_api -> orch : get_fleet_status()
activate orch
orch --> fleet_api : { hubs: [...], summary: {...} }
deactivate orch

fleet_api --> bridge : 200 OK  { hubs: [...], summary: {...} }
deactivate fleet_api

bridge --> client : 200 OK  { hubs: [...], summary: {...} }
deactivate bridge

== 4. Dashboard Renders Fleet Data ==

client -> client : _updateCallbacks.forEach(\ncb(data, null))

client -> dashboard : onFleetUpdate(data, null)
deactivate client

dashboard -> dashboard : _consecutiveErrors = 0
dashboard -> dashboard : _fleetFingerprint(data)\n→ compare with _lastFleetJson
dashboard -> dashboard : renderSidebar(data)\n→ hub list in left panel
dashboard -> dashboard : renderDashboard(data)\n→ hub cards with status

dashboard --> user : Fleet dashboard displayed\nwith hub cards
deactivate dashboard

== 5. Continuous Polling (every 5s) ==

note over client, bridge
  setInterval(poll, 5000) keeps
  fetching /api/fleet/status.
  **_fleetFingerprint** skips re-render
  if data hasn't changed.
end note

@enduml
